---
title: Chocolate Cake Balls
source: Emily
servings: 6
prep time: 1 hour
cook time: 35 minutes
---

Preheat oven to 350 F and grease two 9-inch round #cake pans{}.

Stir together @sugar{2%cups}, @all purpose flour{1.75%cups}, @cocoa powder{0.75%cups}, @baking powder{1.5%tsp}, @baking soda{1.5%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp} in a #large mixing bowl{}.

Add @eggs{2}, @milk{1%cup}, @vegetable oil{0.5%cup}, and @vanilla extract{2%tsp}; beat on medium speed for ~{2%minutes} or until well mixed.

Add @boiling water{1%cup} and stir well — the batter will be very thin — and pour into cake pans. Bake for ~{30-35%minutes} or until a wooden pick comes out clean.

Allow cakes to cool overnight in the refrigerator or in the freezer for ~{3-4%hours}.

Crumble the cooled cake into a #large mixing bowl{}.

Soften the @cream cheese{8%oz} and @butter{4%tbsp} in the microwave, then mix in with cake.

Add @powdered sugar{3%cups} to the cake mixture. Mix well until all ingredients are well-combined.

Roll the cake into small balls and dip in @melting chocolate{2%bags}(melted). Allow cake balls to fully cool.

> Cake balls can be stored in the refrigerator for 1-2 weeks.
